{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20353",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.62,
      "end_seconds": 5.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Mm, morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.42,
      "end_seconds": 11.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.93,
      "end_seconds": 19.0,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Yeah, it's small blisters in a band. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.76,
      "end_seconds": 21.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "When did this begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.1,
      "end_seconds": 29.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Probably two weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.6,
      "end_seconds": 37.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "Sure. And what about vision changes, confusion, rash on the other side or rash near the eye?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.96,
      "end_seconds": 41.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.16,
      "end_seconds": 44.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.65,
      "end_seconds": 48.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.71,
      "end_seconds": 53.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.84,
      "end_seconds": 60.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Years back I got stomach pain from naproxen, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.93,
      "end_seconds": 73.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.99,
      "end_seconds": 77.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Just a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.62,
      "end_seconds": 96.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.87,
      "end_seconds": 100.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.63,
      "end_seconds": 105.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.69,
      "end_seconds": 110.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.12,
      "end_seconds": 114.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.71,
      "end_seconds": 120.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.9,
      "end_seconds": 125.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.77,
      "end_seconds": 131.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.61,
      "end_seconds": 136.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.52,
      "end_seconds": 141.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Right, uh, my grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.4,
      "end_seconds": 153.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.0,
      "end_seconds": 164.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "It's lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day for my pressure. I'm on Dolo, when I get the pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.63,
      "end_seconds": 168.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Right, do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.29,
      "end_seconds": 170.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "650 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.16,
      "end_seconds": 175.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.19,
      "end_seconds": 185.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.09,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.23,
      "end_seconds": 189.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Sure. Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.27,
      "end_seconds": 201.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.98,
      "end_seconds": 222.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "Okay: temp 38.3 degrees, BP is 126 over 77, respiratory rate 20, pulse 88."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.18,
      "end_seconds": 224.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.45,
      "end_seconds": 229.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.0,
      "end_seconds": 234.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.43,
      "end_seconds": 238.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.81,
      "end_seconds": 259.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "There are clustered blisters on a red base in a band across the right side of the chest, not crossing the midline."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.15,
      "end_seconds": 266.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.23,
      "end_seconds": 284.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I don't have a clear answer today: shingles is possible, and so is contact dermatitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.52,
      "end_seconds": 289.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.43,
      "end_seconds": 320.73,
      "duration_seconds": 30.3,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like shingles, but I'd like to confirm. I think a swab from a blister makes sense here, for vesicular rash. For this, aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day, for seven days. That's for shingles. Keep the rash clean and dry and avoid contact with pregnant women or newborns until the blisters crust over."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.39,
      "end_seconds": 338.74,
      "duration_seconds": 17.35,
      "text": "If the rash spreads to the eye or face, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Come back if the pain persists after a month. Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.65,
      "end_seconds": 352.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.58,
      "text": "So, I take the aciclovir, 800 milligrams, five times a day and come back if the pain persists after a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.77,
      "end_seconds": 356.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.27,
      "end_seconds": 361.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.03,
      "end_seconds": 364.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}